// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 03-types/fixed_array_length_non_literal_neg_01.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A fixed-array length must be an integer literal. A struct field reaches the
// checker without the binder's callable-header gate, so the checker's source
// type builder is the single funnel that rejects the length. It must drain as
// ZOM4079 rather than fall through to a signature invariant.
// CHECK: Error [ZOM4079]: Expression is not allowed in a constant value
// CHECK-NEXT:   --> conformance/03-types/fixed_array_length_non_literal_neg_01.zom:2:16
